\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Current along the two paths}
\date{2026-11-06}

\p{\ref{fdip-005U} defines the effective resistance of one edge,
and \ref{fdip-00CS} gives the cycle. Two vertices of that cycle
are joined by two paths, and those paths meet only at the two
vertices. Send one unit of current in at the first vertex and
out at the second. How do the paths share the current, and what
voltage difference does the division produce?}
